{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>You shall not boil a kid … you shall surely tithe.</b> What has this to do with that? The Holy One, blessed be He, said to Israel: Do not cause Me to boil kids of grain while they are still in their mothers' wombs — for if you do not tithe tithes properly when it is about to ripen, I bring an east wind and it blasts them, as it says (II Kings 19) ״וּשְׁדֵפָה לִפְנֵי קָמָה״ — and likewise regarding first-fruits (Pesikta Rabbati; Tanḥuma)." "<b>Year by year.</b> From here: one does not tithe from the new upon the old (Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:05.752607282Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}